text:
ashley: Quick note  opened PR to make function/tool output examples tolerant: migrate from top-level "output" to a nullable "result" envelope. PR: https://git.redwood/infer/docs/pull/901

ashley: Key idea: `result` can be null when the tool produced nothing or failed; when present it contains `payload`, optional `confidence`, and optional `reason` for human context. This reduces brittle failures from tiny model output glitches.

mike: can you paste a compact before/after example?

ashley: sure:
```json
// before
{"tool": "isbn_lookup", "output": {"title": "Infra at Scale"}}
// after
{"tool": "isbn_lookup", "result": {"payload": {"title": "Infra at Scale"}, "confidence": 0.93}}
// or when no result
{"tool": "isbn_lookup", "result": null}
```

priya: couple followups: 1) how do we differentiate transient errors vs legitimately empty responses? 2) what about existing examples used by snapshot tests?

ashley: we added optional `reason` string: e.g. `reason: "timeout"` for transient issues. For tests/examples: plan a migration window where parser tests accept both old `output` and new `result` shapes.

priya: SDK work: i'll add `parseRelaxed()` to TS SDK. It will: try strict JSON parse, run a small sanitizer (trim trailing commas, close unclosed arrays if plausible, wrap bare values into an envelope), then fallback to JSON5. Ill include unit tests for the common noisy outputs we've seen in prod. snippet:```ts
// old
const payload = JSON.parse(resp.text);
// new
const payload = parseRelaxed(resp.text);
```

jordan: i'll grep examples and auto-propose conservative replacements: prefer adding `result.payload` comments rather than rewriting ambiguous prose. will open an examples PR with // REVIEW tags where needed.

doc_bot: CI: docs build queued. Current failure summary: 7 link-check failures and 4 example snapshot diffs referencing `output`. https://ci.redwood/infer/1303

mike: once jordan's PR lands ill run local smoke and CI to validate. also agree with adding a tiny console snippet showing `parseRelaxed()` so users see the recommended client-side shim.

ashley: timeline: land schema + SDK helpers today, examples patch tomorrow. @jordan tag me on the examples PR for a quick sweep. i'll also add a one-paragraph migration note under Structured Outputs describing `result` null semantics and the `reason` field.

jordan: starting the grep now. will be conservative and open a single examples PR with a clear changelog.

priya: will push SDK changes with tests; please hold off merging docs-site until examples PR is linked so we don't surprise CI consumers.

ashley: +1. thanks team. once CI is green i'll merge the PR and ship the short migration blurb. :shipit:
